{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L1.001","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L1","axis_values":{"n_files":"2","format_heterogeneity":"all_text","cross_file_dependency":"independent"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have two short emails. Read both and answer.\n\n--- EMAIL 1 (from logistics) ---\nSubject: Site setup — chairs\nWe confirmed with the rental company; they will deliver 12 chairs to the hall on Friday morning. The chairs are already paid for.\n--- END EMAIL 1 ---\n\n--- EMAIL 2 (from logistics) ---\nSubject: Site setup — tables\nUpdate on tables: we will bring 8 folding tables ourselves on Friday morning. No rental needed.\n--- END EMAIL 2 ---\n\nQuestion: Combining both emails, how many items of furniture (chairs and tables together) will be at the hall on Friday morning?\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"20","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":20,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L1.002","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L1","axis_values":{"n_files":"2","format_heterogeneity":"all_text","cross_file_dependency":"independent"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have two short text files. Read both and answer.\n\n--- FILE: roster_engineering.txt ---\nEngineering team:\n  - Aisha Patel\n  - Diego Romero\n  - Mei Chen\n  - Olu Adebayo\n  - Liam Connor\n  - Hana Sato\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: roster_design.txt ---\nDesign team:\n  - Sven Bergstrom\n  - Camila Rojas\n  - Akira Yamada\n  - Priya Iyer\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: Combining both rosters, how many people are on the engineering and design teams in total? (Names do not overlap between files.)\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"10","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":10,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L1.003","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L1","axis_values":{"n_files":"2","format_heterogeneity":"all_text","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have two short files. Read both and answer.\n\n--- FILE: cookie_recipe.txt ---\nStandard chocolate-chip recipe (yields 24 cookies):\n  - 2 cups flour\n  - 1 cup butter\n  - 2 eggs\n  - 1 cup chocolate chips\n  - 0.75 cup sugar\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: bakery_order.txt ---\nOrder for the school carnival:\n  - 120 chocolate-chip cookies, baked using the standard recipe.\n  - Pickup Saturday at 8 AM.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: How many eggs are required to fulfill the school carnival order?\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"10","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":10,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"120/24 = 5 batches; 5 batches * 2 eggs = 10 eggs."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L1.004","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L1","axis_values":{"n_files":"2","format_heterogeneity":"all_text","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have two short notes. Read both and answer.\n\n--- NOTE A: budget_memo.txt ---\nThe marketing budget for Q3 is $25,000 USD. Use it for campaign spend only.\n--- END NOTE A ---\n\n--- NOTE B: q3_spend_log.txt ---\nQ3 campaign spend charged to the Q3 marketing budget so far:\n  - Banner ad campaign: $7,400\n  - Influencer collaboration: $4,200\n  - Conference booth signage for a marketing campaign: $2,150\n--- END NOTE B ---\n\nQuestion: How many U.S. dollars of the Q3 marketing budget remain unspent?\nOutput only the integer, without commas or a currency symbol.","ground_truth":"11250","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":11250,"tolerance":0,"unit":"USD","require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"25000 - (7400+4200+2150) = 25000 - 13750 = 11,250."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L1.005","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L1","axis_values":{"n_files":"2","format_heterogeneity":"all_text","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have two short documents. Read both and answer.\n\n--- DOC 1: trail_distances.txt ---\nPark trail distances (one-way, km):\n  Cedar Loop: 3.2\n  Marsh Walk: 1.8\n  Ridge Trail: 5.4\n--- END DOC 1 ---\n\n--- DOC 2: hike_log.txt ---\nOn Saturday I hiked the Cedar Loop and the Ridge Trail, both as out-and-back routes (walking each in both directions).\n--- END DOC 2 ---\n\nQuestion: How many kilometers, in total, did I hike on Saturday?\nOutput only the number.","ground_truth":"17.2","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":17.2,"tolerance":0.0001,"unit":"km","require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"(3.2 + 5.4) * 2 = 17.2 km."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L2.001","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_files":"2-5","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have several files describing customers and their orders. Read all of them and answer the question.\n\n--- FILE: customers.csv ---\ncustomer_id,name,tier\nC001,Acme Corp,gold\nC002,Bluefin LLC,silver\nC003,Cedarworks,gold\nC004,Driftwood Inc,bronze\nC005,Evergreen Co,silver\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: orders.csv ---\norder_id,customer_id,amount_usd\nO100,C001,420\nO101,C003,310\nO102,C002,150\nO103,C001,80\nO104,C004,500\nO105,C003,220\nO106,C005,90\nO107,C001,250\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: discounts.md ---\n# Tier discounts\n- gold: 20% discount applied to each order's amount\n- silver: 10% discount\n- bronze: 0% discount (no discount)\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: notes.txt ---\nAll amounts in orders.csv are list prices before tier discount. Final billed amount = list price * (1 - tier discount fraction). Round each invoice to the nearest cent.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: What is the total final billed amount, in U.S. dollars, for all orders placed by customer 'Cedarworks' (i.e., customer C003)?\nOutput only the number, with up to two decimal places, no currency symbol or commas.","ground_truth":"424.00","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":424.0,"tolerance":0.005,"unit":"USD","require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"C003 = Cedarworks = gold (20% off). Orders O101=310, O105=220. Sum=530. After 20% off: 424.00."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L2.002","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_files":"2-5","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have several files describing a small library and recent loans. Answer the question after them.\n\n--- FILE: books.csv ---\nbook_id,title,replacement_cost_usd\nB01,The Midnight Atlas,28\nB02,Galactic Recipes,22\nB03,Stone and Sea,35\nB04,Quiet Engines,40\nB05,Ferns of the Coast,18\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: loans.csv ---\nloan_id,book_id,patron_id,returned\nL1,B01,P10,yes\nL2,B03,P11,no\nL3,B02,P10,yes\nL4,B04,P12,no\nL5,B05,P11,yes\nL6,B01,P12,yes\nL7,B03,P13,yes\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: policy.md ---\n# Lost-book policy\nWhen a book has not been returned within the loan period, the patron is invoiced for the book's replacement cost plus a flat $5 processing fee. The processing fee is per loan, not per book.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: status_note.txt ---\nAll currently unreturned loans (returned == 'no') have exceeded the loan period and are considered lost.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: What is the total amount, in U.S. dollars, that the library should invoice across all currently lost loans?\nOutput only the integer number of dollars (no commas, no currency symbol).","ground_truth":"85","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":85,"tolerance":0,"unit":"USD","require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"Lost: L2 (B03=35) + L4 (B04=40). Each + $5 fee. (35+5) + (40+5) = 40 + 45 = 85."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L2.003","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_files":"2-5","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have a small Python project's files. Read all of them and answer.\n\n--- FILE: README.md ---\n# stockrun\nA tiny utility that reports portfolio totals. Public entry point: `compute_total(holdings)`.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: prices.py ---\nPRICES = {\n    'AAPL': 195.0,\n    'MSFT': 410.0,\n    'GOOG': 170.0,\n    'AMZN': 185.0,\n}\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: holdings.py ---\nHOLDINGS = {\n    'AAPL': 4,\n    'MSFT': 2,\n    'GOOG': 5,\n    'AMZN': 1,\n}\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: stockrun.py ---\nfrom prices import PRICES\n\ndef compute_total(holdings):\n    return sum(PRICES[sym] * qty for sym, qty in holdings.items())\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: run.py ---\nfrom holdings import HOLDINGS\nfrom stockrun import compute_total\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print(compute_total(HOLDINGS))\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: When `python run.py` is executed, what number does it print?\nOutput only the number.","ground_truth":"2635.0","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":2635.0,"tolerance":0.0001,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"195*4 + 410*2 + 170*5 + 185*1 = 780+820+850+185 = 2,635."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L2.004","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_files":"2-5","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"many_to_many_reconciliation"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have several documents about a small conference. Read all of them and answer.\n\n--- FILE: schedule.csv ---\nsession_id,track,start_time,end_time,room\nS1,AI,09:00,10:00,Hall A\nS2,Systems,09:00,10:00,Hall B\nS3,AI,10:30,11:30,Hall A\nS4,Security,10:30,11:30,Hall B\nS5,AI,13:00,14:00,Hall A\nS6,Systems,13:00,14:00,Hall B\nS7,Security,14:30,15:30,Hall A\nS8,AI,14:30,15:30,Hall B\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: speakers.csv ---\nsession_id,speaker\nS1,Mahmoud Rahimi\nS2,Lena Bauer\nS3,Hiroshi Tanaka\nS4,Erika Andersen\nS5,Mahmoud Rahimi\nS6,Pranav Joshi\nS7,Erika Andersen\nS8,Yara Khoury\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: registration_form.md ---\n# Attendee Pranav's plan\nPranav wants to attend every AI-track session he can without leaving Hall A.\nHe cannot attend a session he is also speaking at, and he cannot be in two places\nat once (he cannot attend a session that overlaps in time with another commitment,\nincluding a session he is speaking at).\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: rules.txt ---\nEach session is 60 minutes long. Attendees count one 'session-attended' per session\nthey sit through start to finish. Speakers do not count as attendees of their own session.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: How many sessions, in total, will Pranav attend as an audience member?\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"2","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":2,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"AI in Hall A: S1 (09-10), S3 (10:30-11:30), S5 (13-14). Pranav speaks at S6 (13-14 Hall B), which overlaps with S5. Pranav can attend S1 and S3. Answer = 2."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L2.005","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_files":"2-5","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have several documents about a hardware purchase. Read all of them and answer.\n\n--- FILE: parts_catalog.csv ---\npart_id,name,unit_price_usd,unit_weight_g\nP1,Widget A,4.50,30\nP2,Widget B,7.20,45\nP3,Bracket,2.10,20\nP4,Bolt-pack,1.40,15\nP5,Cable,3.30,25\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: order.csv ---\npart_id,quantity\nP1,10\nP2,4\nP3,20\nP5,6\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: shipping.md ---\n# Shipping\nShipping cost is $0.05 per gram of total package weight.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: tax_note.txt ---\nSales tax of 8% is applied to the subtotal of parts (not to shipping).\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: What is the grand total of the order in U.S. dollars (parts subtotal + tax + shipping)? Round to the nearest cent.\nOutput only the number, with two decimal places, no currency symbol.","ground_truth":"197.95","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A197\\.95\\Z"},"tags":[],"notes":"Subtotal = 10*4.50+4*7.20+20*2.10+6*3.30 = 45+28.80+42+19.80 = 135.60. Tax = 135.60*0.08 = 10.848. Weight = 10*30+4*45+20*20+6*25 = 300+180+400+150 = 1030 g. Shipping = 1030*0.05 = 51.50. Grand total = 135.60+10.848+51.50 = 197.948 → 197.95 (round to cent)."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L3.001","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_files":"6-17","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"many_to_many_reconciliation","context_length":"~356 tokens (chars/4 estimate)"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have many files describing a software release. Read all of them and answer. Historical version headings in CHANGELOG.md describe prior releases and should not be treated as current-version declarations.\n\n--- FILE: pyproject.toml ---\n[project]\nname = \"meridian\"\nversion = \"2.7.4\"\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: src/meridian/__init__.py ---\n__version__ = \"2.7.4\"\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: docs/conf.py ---\nproject = 'Meridian'\nrelease = '2.7.4'\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: CHANGELOG.md ---\n# Changelog\n## 2.7.4 — 2025-04-12\n- Fix: rare race in scheduler.\n- Doc: clarify retry policy.\n## 2.7.3 — 2025-03-30\n- Fix: incorrect timezone in audit log.\n## 2.7.2 — 2025-03-10\n- Feature: SOCKS5 proxy support.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: helm/Chart.yaml ---\napiVersion: v2\nname: meridian\nversion: 2.7.4\nappVersion: \"2.7.5\"\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: package.json ---\n{\n  \"name\": \"@meridian/cli\",\n  \"version\": \"2.7.4\"\n}\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: docker-compose.yml ---\nservices:\n  meridian:\n    image: meridian:2.7.4\n    ports:\n      - 8080:8080\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: README.md ---\n# Meridian\nLatest release: **2.7.4**. See CHANGELOG.md for details.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: The current release version declared across the project metadata is 2.7.4. Ignoring historical changelog headings, one file additionally declares an application version of 2.7.5. Which file is it? Reply with the file's path exactly as shown above.","ground_truth":"helm/Chart.yaml","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"helm/Chart.yaml","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["context_length_relabelled"],"notes":"Chart.yaml has appVersion 2.7.5 while every other reference is 2.7.4."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L3.002","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_files":"6-17","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"many_to_many_reconciliation"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have many files describing a small fleet of delivery trucks. Read all and answer.\n\n--- FILE: fleet.csv ---\ntruck_id,model,capacity_kg\nT1,Helix-300,3000\nT2,Helix-300,3000\nT3,Helix-500,5000\nT4,Helix-500,5000\nT5,Helix-800,8000\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: drivers.csv ---\ndriver_id,name,assigned_truck_id\nD1,Olufemi Bello,T1\nD2,Mei Chen,T2\nD3,Ravi Sharma,T3\nD4,Helga Strom,T4\nD5,Jovan Petrov,T5\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: routes_monday.csv ---\ndriver_id,packages,total_weight_kg\nD1,28,2400\nD2,15,1100\nD3,42,4600\nD4,38,5400\nD5,55,7200\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: routes_tuesday.csv ---\ndriver_id,packages,total_weight_kg\nD1,30,2900\nD2,18,1300\nD3,45,4900\nD4,40,4800\nD5,52,7800\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: rules.md ---\n# Loading rules\nA truck is **overloaded** on a given day if its total weight (kg) for that day exceeds its capacity. Each driver uses only their assigned truck.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: incident_log.txt ---\nAll overload incidents on Monday and Tuesday are reportable.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: Across Monday and Tuesday combined, how many distinct (driver_id, day) pairs represent an overload incident?\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"1","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":1,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":[],"notes":"Capacities: T1=3000,T2=3000,T3=5000,T4=5000,T5=8000. Mon weights: D1 2400(<3000), D2 1100(<3000), D3 4600(<5000), D4 5400(>5000 OVER), D5 7200(<8000). Tue weights: D1 2900(<3000), D2 1300(<3000), D3 4900(<5000), D4 4800(<5000), D5 7800(<8000). Only D4 Mon → 1 incident."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L3.003","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_files":"6-17","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have many documents about a class roster, exam scores, and grading policy. Read all of them and answer.\n\n--- FILE: students.csv ---\nstudent_id,name,section\nS01,Aria Ferraro,A\nS02,Bilal Hassan,A\nS03,Chenxi Wu,B\nS04,Dimitri Volkov,B\nS05,Elif Yilmaz,A\nS06,Farouk N'Diaye,B\nS07,Greta Holm,A\nS08,Hiroshi Mori,B\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: midterm.csv ---\nstudent_id,score\nS01,82\nS02,71\nS03,90\nS04,55\nS05,88\nS06,67\nS07,95\nS08,73\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: final.csv ---\nstudent_id,score\nS01,78\nS02,80\nS03,92\nS04,60\nS05,84\nS06,72\nS07,90\nS08,70\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: grading_policy.md ---\n# Course grade\ncourse_grade = 0.4 * midterm + 0.6 * final\nLetter grade thresholds (course_grade in 0–100):\n  A: ≥ 85\n  B: 70 ≤ grade < 85\n  C: 60 ≤ grade < 70\n  F: < 60\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: section_a_note.txt ---\nSection A is the morning section. Section B is the afternoon section.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: enrollment_note.txt ---\nAll eight students completed both exams; no withdrawals.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: How many students earned a letter grade of A (course_grade ≥ 85)?\nOutput only the integer.","ground_truth":"3","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":3,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["weighted_average","threshold_count","csv_join","multi_document_reasoning"],"notes":"0.4*M + 0.6*F: S01: 0.4*82+0.6*78 = 32.8+46.8 = 79.6 → B. S02: 0.4*71+0.6*80 = 28.4+48 = 76.4 → B. S03: 0.4*90+0.6*92 = 36+55.2 = 91.2 → A. S04: 0.4*55+0.6*60 = 22+36 = 58 → F. S05: 0.4*88+0.6*84 = 35.2+50.4 = 85.6 → A. S06: 0.4*67+0.6*72 = 26.8+43.2 = 70 → B. S07: 0.4*95+0.6*90 = 38+54 = 92 → A. S08: 0.4*73+0.6*70 = 29.2+42 = 71.2 → B. A count = S03,S05,S07 = 3."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L3.004","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_files":"6-17","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have many documents related to a small chess tournament. Read all and answer.\n\n--- FILE: players.csv ---\nplayer_id,name\nP1,Alma Vance\nP2,Bran Doyle\nP3,Cora Singh\nP4,Dario Lin\nP5,Esra Yildiz\nP6,Finn Holub\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: round1_results.csv ---\nwhite_id,black_id,result\nP1,P4,1-0\nP2,P5,0-1\nP3,P6,1/2-1/2\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: round2_results.csv ---\nwhite_id,black_id,result\nP1,P5,1/2-1/2\nP4,P6,1-0\nP3,P2,1-0\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: round3_results.csv ---\nwhite_id,black_id,result\nP5,P3,1/2-1/2\nP6,P1,0-1\nP2,P4,1/2-1/2\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: scoring.md ---\n# Scoring\n- Win = 1 point.\n- Draw = 0.5 points each.\n- Loss = 0 points.\nResult format is 'white-black'. So '1-0' means white wins; '0-1' means black wins; '1/2-1/2' means a draw.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: tiebreakers.md ---\n# Tie-breakers\nTie-breakers are not used for the question below; ranking is by total points only.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: schedule_overview.txt ---\nRound 1 was played Friday evening. Round 2 was played Saturday morning. Round 3 was played Saturday afternoon. All players appeared in all three rounds.\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: notes.txt ---\nThe tournament has six players and three rounds. Standings rank by total points descending.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: After all three rounds, who is the sole player with the highest total points?\nReply with that player's full name exactly as written in players.csv.","ground_truth":"Alma Vance","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Alma Vance","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["chess","table_aggregation","cross_document_reconciliation","exact_answer"],"notes":"Across 8 files. Round-by-round: P1: R1 W1.0 + R2 D0.5 + R3 W1.0 = 2.5. P2: R1 L + R2 L + R3 D0.5 = 0.5. P3: R1 D0.5 + R2 W1.0 + R3 D0.5 = 2.0. P4: R1 L + R2 W1.0 + R3 D0.5 = 1.5. P5: R1 W1.0 + R2 D0.5 + R3 D0.5 = 2.0. P6: R1 D0.5 + R2 L + R3 L = 0.5. P1 = 2.5 is sole leader → Alma Vance."}
{"probe_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis.L3.005","canonical_id":"longctx.multi_document_synthesis","category":"longctx","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_files":"6-17","format_heterogeneity":"mixed_text_table","cross_file_dependency":"joinable_keys"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have many documents describing a small e-commerce inventory. Read all and answer.\n\n--- FILE: products.csv ---\nsku,name,unit_price_usd\nK01,Pewter Kettle,45.00\nK02,Cast-iron Pan,38.00\nK03,Glass Carafe,22.00\nK04,Bamboo Cutting Board,18.00\nK05,Ceramic Mug,12.00\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: stock_warehouse_a.csv ---\nsku,units\nK01,40\nK02,25\nK03,80\nK04,60\nK05,200\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: stock_warehouse_b.csv ---\nsku,units\nK01,15\nK02,30\nK03,40\nK04,50\nK05,150\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: stock_warehouse_c.csv ---\nsku,units\nK01,10\nK02,20\nK03,60\nK04,40\nK05,100\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: open_orders.csv ---\norder_id,sku,units\nO1,K01,5\nO2,K02,12\nO3,K03,40\nO4,K05,100\nO5,K04,30\nO6,K02,18\nO7,K05,60\nO8,K03,30\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: policy.md ---\n# Inventory accounting\nAvailable stock for an SKU = total units across all warehouses minus the total units reserved by all open orders for that SKU.\nInventory value = sum over all SKUs of (available_stock * unit_price).\n--- END FILE ---\n\n--- FILE: note.txt ---\nThere are exactly three warehouses (A, B, C) and no other stock locations. Open orders represent units that are reserved but not yet shipped.\n--- END FILE ---\n\nQuestion: What is the total **available** inventory value, in U.S. dollars?\nOutput only the number, with up to two decimal places, no currency symbol or commas.","ground_truth":"12470.00","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A12470(?:\\.0{1,2})?\\Z"},"tags":["inventory_accounting","cross_document_aggregation","numeric_reasoning"],"notes":"Warehouse totals: K01=40+15+10=65; K02=25+30+20=75; K03=80+40+60=180; K04=60+50+40=150; K05=200+150+100=450. Reserved: K01=5; K02=12+18=30; K03=40+30=70; K04=30; K05=100+60=160. Available: K01=60; K02=45; K03=110; K04=120; K05=290. Value: 60*45.00 + 45*38.00 + 110*22.00 + 120*18.00 + 290*12.00 = 2700+1710+2420+2160+3480 = 12,470.00."}
